docs/architecture.md:39:Attached status marks are simulation state: their chosen part positions, rotations, variants, and replacement lifetime stay stable across frames and inactive fields. `SwfTankStatusView` consumes those choices without drawing random values or changing game rules. It holds variant frames while allowing nested clips to animate and applies the recovered infection color matrix to the complete tank view. Screen ink is an independently queued global effect; its lifetime and overlap do not belong to an avatar.
docs/architecture.md:193:`simulation/tank-display.ts` records semantic direct-child order without browser objects. This order affects the source forcefield passive's readiness, so part registration, shield/status attachment and ordinary cleanup update it in the simulation. `TankView` consumes the same tokens to order parts, status marks and protection, keeping each forcefield splash/mask pair together. Arrival clears shield immunity independently of its surviving film and stage clock. The current registry still represents the shared shield view; independent shield instances remain a later checkpoint.
docs/fidelity.md:109:- `_-14/_-6.as` freezes Apocalypse at the visual bubble wall while its fuse runs; it does not immediately kill the field. `_-MC` (2173) ends after 120 frames; `_-0D.ShrinkBubblefield` subtracts 1/204 scale each frame. The implementation marks the field destroyed and escapes at the end. Reward/transition choreography still needs a runtime comparison.
docs/fidelity.md:118:- `_-Zx.EffectMeCrazy` replaces earlier marks, places one per part below five parts, and otherwise picks five parts with replacement. Sticky/jam/weaken hold a randomized variant while nested clips keep playing; stun plays from a randomized starting frame. `_-U4` supplies the infection overlay, random rotation, and color matrix. `_-ar` applies ink only to the avatar without refreshing an existing timer; a forcefield suppresses its visual effect while retaining its timer. The ink clip has its own authored 100-frame lifetime.
