docs/fidelity.md:204:- `_‑ct/_‑LM`4021 records raw references per mounted gun. Its eighth reference emits1834 at the oldest object's current position, shifts the reference, and marks the object to skip its next Run before removal. Ordinary removal leaves those raw references stale because generic cleanup expects `.mc`; `_‑0D:1202` and pcode5249 confirm the caught owner-level mismatch. `_‑ct/_‑J2`4009 instead stores `{mc,x,y}` wrappers, cleans the first matching reference and uses birth coordinates on cap expiry. Cleanup aborts the current owner's remaining guns on an invalid/raw `.mc`, then continues to the next enemy owner. Suppressed transit spawns still enter the lists; a null oldest is guarded instead of deliberately throwing the source's null dereference. This bounded exception is explicit.
